{
  "id": "COMPOUND:5426 - PROTEIN:4886",
  "verbalization": "Lumiliximab is implicated in the activation of Serine/threonine-protein kinase ATR through multiple indirect pathways. The drug targets two distinct enzymes—Endothelial lipase and Peptide deformylase—each of which is itself a target of another compound. Endothelial lipase is inhibited by Macluraxanthone B, which in turn activates ATR, while Peptide deformylase is targeted by Albinoside Ii and 2-(3,4-Dimethoxyphenyl)-5,7-Dihydroxychromen-4-One, both of which also lead to ATR activation. These pathways collectively suggest that Lumiliximab may influence ATR through a series of enzyme-target interactions, potentially modulating kinase activity in a downstream biological process. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Lumiliximab and ATR, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
